      "id": "b2",
      "function": "problem",
      "scene_type": "rv_board",
      "spoken": "Eighteen sixty: Lenoir's engine ignites its gas mixture without compressing it first. According to an MIT lecture it manages ten cycles a minute and less than five percent efficiency. About five hundred are sold. That sounds poor, but it was a start. There is no compression stroke at all.",
