      "id": "b5",
      "function": "insight",
      "scene_type": "rv_board",
      "spoken": "An example built in eighteen sixty-nine by Crossley in Manchester is in the Science Museum today. The museum calls the Otto and Langen engine the world's first commercially successful internal combustion engine. We cover the next big step on Sunday: compressing before igniting. Seven years made a big difference.",
